  "body": "**A PathPilot plasma post for the Tormach 1300PL.**\n\nWords from [UM10720](https://tormach.com/media/asset/u/m/um10720_1300pl_1223a_web.pdf) §6–7 and Tormach's [post guidelines](https://knowledgebase.tormach.com/8l/pathpilot-post-processor-guidelines):\n- **Preamble:** `G20|G21 / G90 / G64 P<inch> / G17 / G54.. / G43 H1 / G30`. G64 P is always in inches.\n- **Per contour:** `G0` to the lead-in start, then `M200` (AutoFS; or M207/M208/M209/M210/M211 plus F when the op states them), `G15` (probe), `G16` (pierce + THC on), the XY `G1`/`G2`/`G3` path, `M205` (torch off and back to G30 Z), `G30`.\n- **End:** `G30` then `M30`.\n- **Refused by name:** M3/M4/M5/M7/M8/M9, any Z cutting move, G95/G96.\n- **M6 conflict:** the manual's example uses `T1 M6`, but the guidelines list M6 as unsupported on plasma. It's resolved by **omitting M6** and noting it, pending a Hub or real-machine run.\n- **No program delimiters** (`%`).\n\n**Done means:**\n- the post writes the per-contour block exactly;\n- refusals are pinned;\n- a golden `.nc` exists for a plate with an outer profile and two holes;\n- a PathPilot Hub (1300PL) run is requested from the contributor before trusting it on a machine.\n\nPart of #621\n",
